WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.917
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.193
I see braids.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.173
- I'm gonna fly on a plane

00:00:05.173 --> 00:00:06.590
with my two-and-a-half-year-old daughter

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.853
to Virginia without my wife.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.467
Flynn, we're going on
an airplane tomorrow.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.300
- [Flynn] Huh?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.603
- We had a trip planned
to go to Austin, Texas,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.610
one last trip before our
second child arrives,

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.840
but my grandmother passed away

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.380
and I needed to go to
Virginia to be with my family.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.530
Do you think I'll be fine, Kate?

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.630
Traveling with Flynn alone on an airplane?

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:25.899
- I do think it's a lot.

00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:27.507
- Kate's gonna stay in California

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.310
and we're gonna meet up in Austin, Texas,

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.160
for Mother's Day.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.313
This might be a disaster.

00:00:33.393 --> 00:00:34.584
(crying)

00:00:34.584 --> 00:00:36.230
Flynn, we're gonna see Mom in Texas.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.440
Flynn could stay with Kate,

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.020
but I really want Flynn to see my mom

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.743
and dad and brothers and sisters.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.320
I'm Filipino, and I really want Flynn

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.920
to grow up proud to be Filipino.

00:00:44.135 --> 00:00:46.718
(bright music)

00:00:47.121 --> 00:00:49.671
- [Announcer] A-31 through 60, gates--

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.010
- Alright, made it to the airport.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.980
Got the car seat and the diaper bag

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.720
in one big, old bag on my back.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.500
Flynn seems a little sad.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.790
As a kid I was a mama's boy,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.057
so I totally sympathize with Flynn.

00:01:01.057 --> 00:01:03.640
(bright music)

00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:06.808
(Flynn babbling)

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.620
While the plane is
reaching cruising altitude,

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.723
we're not allowed to use the seat tray,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.590
so I kind of hacked together this way

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:16.143
to hold the iPad up.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.763
But now Flynn doesn't wanna
sit in the car seat anymore.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.260
Luckily Flynn is taking a nap.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.950
It's a few hours past her normal nap time,

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.230
but she's napping.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.573
When the plane lands, she's excited.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.920
- We made it to Baltimore.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.320
Now, we gotta get to Norfolk

00:01:33.839 --> 00:01:37.900
and gotta say, the car
seat was an accident.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.563
Found an errant smart cart.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:45.259
(Flynn babbling)

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.163
Got some fries for Flynn.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.850
We gate check the car seat,

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.690
and it's a lot less stressful

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.900
getting Flynn onto the plane

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.000
without having to lug around the car seat.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.340
Don't pick your nose.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.110
We're here in Norfolk.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:07.980
Say hi to Auntie Maya.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.180
Can you give her a hug?
- Hi, Flynn!

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.013
- You scared?

00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:15.713
Now, Flynn is pretty shy around my dad.

00:02:16.085 --> 00:02:17.740
What is it?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:18.873
We call him Lolo.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.010
Flynn only gets to see my
parents maybe once a year,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.110
so she doesn't really know them that well.

00:02:25.764 --> 00:02:27.403
Are you happy to see Auntie Maya?

00:02:28.101 --> 00:02:28.938
- Hi, Flynn.

00:02:28.938 --> 00:02:31.521
(Flynn laughs)

00:02:32.793 --> 00:02:34.553
- You're really happy, very happy.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.163
It's 10:30 in Norfolk, east coast time,

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.000
which is 7:30 California time,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.610
so Flynn woke up right on time,

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.660
even though you went to bed a little late.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.493
You hungry?

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.383
What do you wanna get?

00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:56.677
What do you wanna get?
- Bear!

00:02:56.677 --> 00:02:57.963
- You can't eat a bear!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.780
The memorial for my grandma
isn't until tomorrow,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.460
but I want to see my
family as much as possible

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.273
the few days that we're here.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.903
We're gonna go see Uncle John.

00:03:07.647 --> 00:03:09.383
- Uncle John.
- Yeah, my brother.

00:03:11.216 --> 00:03:12.049
- Hey!

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.690
- Uncle John!
- No.

00:03:15.566 --> 00:03:17.983
(soft music)

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.393
- Who's that?

00:03:21.419 --> 00:03:23.616
- Hey!

00:03:23.616 --> 00:03:27.449
I'm so glad you could
come, hello, who's that?

00:03:27.652 --> 00:03:31.485
(talking in foreign language)

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.010
- So, I called up my mom two weeks ago

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.850
to wish her a happy birthday,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.640
and it was that day that I found out

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.853
that my grandma was on her deathbed.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.713
My mom was staying beside her all night,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.903
Just to be around, in case she passed.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.310
So, everyone's coming over

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.510
to where Flynn and I
are staying for dinner,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.750
and Flynn's cousins and my older brother

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.407
are there and they get to hang out.

00:03:58.407 --> 00:03:59.910
- Hey!
- Hi, uncle Mark

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.473
Flynn's pretty shy around
her cousins at first,

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.210
- You can't just grab him
with his hand like that.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.380
- But it doesn't take her long

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.563
to hold her hands and have fun.

00:04:09.911 --> 00:04:11.840
(children talking)

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.500
Pretty soon, a lot of
my family comes over,

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.020
including my younger sister Anna,

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.520
who I haven't seen in a while,

00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:18.770
(children yelling)

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.470
It's definitely crowded and it reminds me

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.793
a lot of growing up.

00:04:23.114 --> 00:04:25.830
(family talking loudly)

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.110
We weren't surrounded by a
large Filipino community,

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.363
so my family were the
Filipinos that I knew.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.620
As a kid, being of a different culture,

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.550
it could be lonely, it can be kinda scary

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.150
when people become hostile.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.470
So, I always felt safe around
my family and you know,

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.803
I want Flynn to have that same comfort.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.950
I wish we could do this more often.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.840
You're kind of tossing and turning,

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.104
but you got to sleep.

00:04:54.104 --> 00:04:54.937
- Cousins!

00:04:55.306 --> 00:04:56.139
Cousins!

00:04:56.139 --> 00:04:57.115
- You want to see your cousins?

00:04:57.115 --> 00:04:57.948
- Yeah!

00:04:57.948 --> 00:04:59.790
- The whole trip started
out pretty stressful,

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.503
but I've adapted, Flynn's has adapted,

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.870
We both miss Kate, but you know,

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.800
we're having a pretty good time.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.753
You're doing it!

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.660
Today's my grandmother's memorial,

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.453
and Flynn gets to hang out
with her cousins some more.

00:05:16.037 --> 00:05:18.050
♪ Ring around the rosie ♪

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.760
- My grandma used to call my siblings

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.463
and I her little branches.

00:05:21.604 --> 00:05:25.687
♪ Ashes, ashes, we all fall down ♪

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.053
- And I guess Flynn is, you
know, an extension of that.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.090
My grandma, my grandpa used
to play music together.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.593
Flynn gets to experience, you know,

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.090
us being musical together
and having a good time.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.410
Giving her that exposure
to the Filipino side

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.270
of my family is really important to me.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:48.060
I think I'm finally
able to process the fact

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.493
that my grandma's not
in this world anymore.

00:05:51.554 --> 00:05:54.137
(somber music)

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.430
It's Mother's Day and
my brothers and sisters,

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.900
and my mom and dad and Flynn's cousins

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.370
get to come with use to
the airport to send us off.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:09.633
I'm glad I got to tell my
mom happy Mother's Day.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.250
It does feel different, you
know, with my grandma gone.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.900
Like, my mom's the new matriarch.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.480
I've had a lot of fun
with just Flynn and I.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.970
I'm so happy that Flynn got
to hang out with my family.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.720
She's gonna miss her cousins a lot.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.200
But, she also misses
Kate a lot and I do, too.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.630
So, that's gonna be really
awesome to see Kate,

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.330
and wish her a happy Mother's Day.

00:06:29.425 --> 00:06:30.258
- Mom!

00:06:33.603 --> 00:06:34.686
- [Kate] Yay!

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.611
- [Dad] Happy Mother's Day!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.210
- I'm excited to see
you, Flynn, I missed you.

00:06:45.987 --> 00:06:47.070
- Missed you.

00:06:47.885 --> 00:06:50.468
(somber music)

